{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", "label": "Failure Taxonomy", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named failure modes, so a failing run can be classified rather than described. Every mode has a detection column: a mode you cannot detect from a recording is a mode you cannot count."}, {"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f11_substituted_answer", "label": "F11 \u2014 Substituted Answer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asked for an average bonus from a column that does not exist, the model computed the average salary, wrote it, and reported success with no hedge. 3/5 seeds."}, {"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f8_over_eager_write", "label": "F8 \u2014 Over-Eager Write", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The milder version and arguably more troubling: it said the column was missing, then wrote a placeholder anyway. It knew, and produced a file regardless."}, {"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f12_partial_constraint_application", "label": "F12 \u2014 Partial Constraint Application", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every failing seed wrote 5 where the answer is 4 \u2014 off by exactly one, always the same direction. Systematic, not noise, which is why the task discriminates."}, {"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_j1_judge_instability", "label": "J1 \u2014 Judge Instability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "summarise-data scored 3/5, 5/5 and 4/5 across three runs on answers verified correct by hand. The judge disagreed with itself, not the agent."}, {"id": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_nothing_is_tuned_to_make_these_pass", "label": "Nothing In The Harness Is Changed To Make These Pass", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They are findings about the model, recorded as such. Tuning the suite until the numbers improve is how a benchmark stops meaning anything."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", "target": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f11_substituted_answer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", "target": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f8_over_eager_write", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", "target": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_f12_partial_constraint_application", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", "target": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_j1_judge_instability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evals/failure-taxonomy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evals_failure_taxonomy_failure_taxonomy", 